        "deck": "Class-3.pptx",
        "slide": "ppt/slides/slide27.xml",
        "text": "Getting started with Grasshopper Grasshopper started its life as a plugin for Rhino which you had to download and install separately. Since version 6, Rhino now has Grasshopper built-in, so if you are using Rhino 6 or later, you don\u2019t need to install any additional software to use Grasshopper. You can start Grasshopper either by clicking the Grasshopper button in the toolbar or by typing Grasshopper in the Command line."
      }
    ]
  },
